  "caption": "Quinn bought a posture strap at 1am. Strap on: upright. Strap off: straight back to slouching.\n\nPosture straps mostly work as a reminder, and that effect tends to fade once they come off. Aches are often linked more to staying still for too long, low strength, poor sleep and stress than to one \"perfect\" position.\n\nWhat can help: change position every 30–45 minutes, strengthen the upper back with rows, band pull-aparts and carries twice a week, set the screen at eye height with forearms supported, and use phone reminders instead of a strap.\n\nPain that hangs around or one-sided changes are worth getting checked. Braces for a medical condition are best used with professional guidance.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
